Subject: [PATCH] A block is validated with its code protected: a write just before is not lost

DBGetBlock validates a block whose page was written (its jump-table entry is jmpnext) by hashing
its x86 code and, when the hash is the same, protecting the code and putting the block back in the
jump table. The hash was taken before the protection: another thread's write that landed in
between (the page is still writable then) raised no fault and marked nothing, and the block went
back into the jump table with code that is no longer there, for good.

.NET writes a method's precode once (call PrecodeFixupThunk becomes a jump to the compiled code)
and from then on sends callers to the precode. Two threads that call a new method at the same
time hit this: the one that compiled it patched the precode while the other was validating the
old block, and both then ran the old precode, the prestub found the method compiled and sent them
back to the precode, for ever, each at a full core (the official PD2 launcher's two spinning
".NET ThreadPool" threads).

The hash is now taken again after the protection; on a change the block is marked again
(unprotectDB) and this entry runs without it. A write after the protection faults as before.
---
--- a/src/dynarec/dynablock.c
+++ b/src/dynarec/dynablock.c
@@ -516,6 +516,12 @@
                     if(db->always_test==2) {
                         db->always_test = 0;
                         protectDB((uintptr_t)db->x64_addr, db->x64_size);
+                        // as below: a write between the hash and the protection
+                        if(X31_hash_code((void*)db->x64_readaddr, db->x64_size)!=db->hash) {
+                            unprotectDB((uintptr_t)db->x64_addr, db->x64_size, 1);
+                            db->always_test = 2;
+                            db = NULL;
+                        }
                     }
                     // always_test==1 (NEVERCLEAN): skip protectDB, the page has mixed
                     // code+data and mprotect would strip writability from data regions
@@ -529,6 +535,16 @@
                     }
                     #endif
                     protectDBJumpTable((uintptr_t)db->x64_addr, db->x64_size, db->block, db->jmpnext);
+                    // The hash above was taken before the protection. Another thread's write that
+                    // landed in between (on a page still writable) raised no fault and marked
+                    // nothing, so the block would stay in the jump table with code that is no
+                    // longer there (.NET patches a method's precode once: a thread that then runs
+                    // the old precode calls the prestub for ever). Hash again now that a later
+                    // write faults; on a change, mark the block again and run the new code.
+                    if(X31_hash_code((void*)db->x64_readaddr, db->x64_size)!=db->hash) {
+                        unprotectDB((uintptr_t)db->x64_addr, db->x64_size, 1);
+                        db = NULL;
+                    }
                 }
             }
         }
